        Provide a response strictly in the following format:
        Code statements:
        <text1>
        <text2>
        ...
        <textN>

Code statements:
```c
if (READ_ONCE(msk->snd_data_fin_enable) && !(ssk->sk_shutdown & SEND_SHUTDOWN)) {
    gfp_t saved_allocation = ssk->sk_allocation;

    /* we are in a atomic (BH) scope, override ssk default for data
     * fin allocation
     */
    ssk->sk_allocation = GFP_ATOMIC;
    ssk->sk_shutdown |= SEND_SHUTDOWN;
    tcp_shutdown(ssk, SEND_SHUTDOWN);
    ssk->sk_allocation = saved_allocation;
}
```

Code statements:
```c
if (READ_ONCE(msk->snd_data_fin_enable) && !(ssk->sk_shutdown & SEND_SHUTDOWN)) {
    gfp_t saved_allocation = ssk->sk_allocation;

    /* we are in a atomic (BH) scope, override ssk default for data
     * fin allocation
     */
    ssk->sk_allocation = GFP_ATOMIC;
    ssk->sk_shutdown |= SEND_SHUTDOWN;
    tcp_shutdown(ssk, SEND_SHUTDOWN);
    ssk->sk_allocation = saved_allocation;
}
```

The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (READ_ONCE(msk->snd_data_fin_enable) && !(ssk->sk_shutdown & SEND_SHUTDOWN)) {
    ...
    tcp_shutdown(ssk, SEND_SHUTDOWN);
}
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the condition to check if the MPTCP socket is in a shutdown state (`ssk->sk_shutdown & SEND_SHUTDOWN`) is not properly handled before attempting to shut down the TCP connection. If the MPTCP socket is already shut down before the fallback to TCP, the TCP connection remains open, leading to a race condition.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (READ_ONCE(msk->snd_data_fin_enable) && !(ssk->sk_shutdown & SEND_SHUTDOWN)) {
    ...
    tcp_shutdown(ssk, SEND_SHUTDOWN);
}
```
Reason:
The fix explicitly checks the shutdown state of the MPTCP socket (`ssk->sk_shutdown & SEND_SHUTDOWN`) before proceeding with the TCP shutdown. This ensures that if the MPTCP socket has already been shut down, the TCP connection will not be left open, thus preventing the race condition

